 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) Old default scrapping mode: **Scrapping & UnitAI production quotas (generalized)**: Reworked scrapping across (almost) all `UnitAI` types to stop destroy→rebuild loops. Paired with per-`UnitAI` **max/quotas** in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and scrapping guards in `CvUnit::canScrap`. Policy examples: during **war/danger**, suppress explorers/settlers and redirect output to land units; on **naval-heavy** maps (archipelago, etc.) **don’t restrict naval quotas** — sea control can decide wars (e.g., a frigate that sinks transports before they land can neutralize a four-unit invasion) and supports diverse strategies; on **land-heavy** maps (pangaea/continents) set naval quotas **much lower**. In war/danger, naval production quotas drop (sometimes to **0**), but **existing** ships aren’t auto-scrapped; **workers** use a **decaying max** so late-game excess can be scrapped conservatively. Fixes the "naval dementia" case (mass privateers/galleons while land cities fall). See [KI#53](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#53---beyond-tremendously-improved-naval-dementia-of-producing-privateersgalleons-then-seemingly-scrapping-them-and-repeat-orand-of-more-importantly-building-galleons-and-privateers-in-droves-and-excess-if-i-may-say-but-despite-enemy-threatening-cities-of-land-capture-for-20-turns-and-losing-capital-as-a-result-fixedaddressed-by-now-managing-production-of-each-unitai-with-max-by-type-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-as-well-as-disallowing-scrapping-and-managing-it-by-unitai-type-globally-as-well-in-cvunitcanscrap-by-type-as-well-with-max-and-such-other-conditions-for-some-units-like-as-of-now-workers) (complements [KI#52](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#52---beyond-tremendously-improved-remove-ai-scrapping-of-military-land-units-as-way-too-many-units-are-scrapped-early-yet-we-really-need-them-to-defend-against-barbarians-or-our-rivals-or-such)). **Guardrail impact:** likely also covers hidden loops such as the **workboat infinite loop**; see [KI#23](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#23---seemingly-now-fixed-major-bug-of-ai-cities-being-stuck-in-a-loop-of-producing-a-workboat-and-instantly-scrapping-it-so-without-producing-a-new-unit-if-im-not-mistaken-then-producing-a-new-one-endlessly-for-dozen-turns-until-it-somehow-solved-itself-but-way-too-late).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5950+) **Work Boat overproduction bug follow-up:** after fixing the old Work Boat produce/scrap loop, BBAI logs still showed some minor remaining Work Boat overproduction, confirmed by ingame advisors (e.g., Augustus having built 34 Work Boats by T373, more than any other unit type). Two mismatches were fixed. First, cities could decide whether to build a Work Boat using a different water area than the one used to count seafood targets, so need and availability did not always match. Second, Work Boats could skip owned **off-BFC seafood** even though city production had counted it as a valid target. These mismatches are now fixed. Following this, Work Boat production is reduced (e.g., to ~27-29 Work Boats for Augusts, remaining seeming to be due to heavy pillaging). As an extra enhancement, stale Work Boats now also skip seafood already connected by another Work Boat. Following these fixes. See [KI#157](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#157---fixeddiagnosed-base-advciv-bug-minor-ai-work-boat-excess-after-previous-spam-fixes-compare-need-to-the-counted-water-areas-let-sea-workers-resolve-off-bfc-sea-bonuses-and-confirm-many-repeated-rebuilds-were-genuine-net-losses).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) Old default scrapping mode: **Exception: Allow scrapping** for units that have an `ObsoleteTech`: they are less efficient to keep. **Gated strictly** by **domain/era:** (e.g., an archer is not useful at medieval era, but a knight unit is still useful at industrial era). These are **raw XML-cost gates** (no game-speed scaling). Also added a naval exception: **sea units carrying cargo are never scrapped** (e.g., a galley is still useful to transport units).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5979+) **Obsolete-unit scrapping exception:** units that have an `ObsoleteTech` can be scrapped once the active scrap mode allows obsolete cleanup, because very outdated units are less efficient to keep. **Cargo-capable units are kept** because an obsolete transport can still be our only practical way to move units.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) Old default scrapping mode: **Scrapping safeguards**: added pre-checks to stop scrapping **useful units**—**all land military units are protected**, and **no unit can be scrapped before turn 150**. Fixes early "produce then scrap" cases (e.g., macemen) and keeps forces on the map vs. barbarians/rivals (**no economy check**). See **[KI#52](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#52---beyond-tremendously-improved-remove-ai-scrapping-of-military-land-units-as-way-too-many-units-are-scrapped-early-yet-we-really-need-them-to-defend-against-barbarians-or-our-rivals-or-such)**.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) Old default scrapping mode: Add **scrap tolerance beyond unit support costs**: we expect to lose a few units during war; having a few **extra units** helps us not become weaker than our rivals; overshooting may lead to bankruptcy. Formula: `mult * (era + 1) + add` extra units.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) Old default scrapping mode: Heavily increase the importance of **XML Unit Cost (Hammers)** (reliable reflection of a unit's overall strength: e.g. A 4 Strength Trebuchet at 80 Hammers Cost is stronger than a 5 Strength Axeman at 35 Hammers) when deciding which unit to scrap first, and **reduce the importance of experience**: A 0 XP swordsman is more valuable than a 10 XP we will likely never upgrade. Also **account for map heaviness** (e.g. prioritize scrapping land units on archipelago, or galleys on pangea). Change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_disbandValue`.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) **AI scrapping update:** added an optional (as of now disabled) absolute XML kill switch to disable all AI scrapping for testing or preference. This is separate from the normal scrapping optimization toggle, so disabling optimization does not accidentally restore old broad scrapping.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) **AI scrapping update (as of now gates the old default scrapping rules):** block all AI scrapping, **except for units that have been obsolete for one or a few eras**. Example: as of now Axemen obsolete at Civil Service can still be useful through Medieval, but can be scrapped from Renaissance; Knights obsolete in Renaissance can remain useful through Renaissance, but can be scrapped from Industrial. **Cargo-capable units are still kept**, and obsolete candidates **still pass through** the existing XML-cost/domain gates. The rationale is that only very outdated units are no longer useful enough to justify their clutter or upkeep; until then, keeping units is usually better than short-term financial relief from scrapping, because they can defend cities, deter attacks, pressure rivals, or be spent in war. War can also reduce excess units naturally, and successful captures can increase unit support, economy, and long-term growth more than deleting troops would. So this strict-but-not-absolute new scrapping gate is believed to be stronger for AI (at least in theory; in autoplay it does not seem weaker at a glance and based on the now enhanced BBAI logging we added as well).
