+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5945+) **AI scrapping update:** block all AI scrapping, **except for units that have been obsolete for one or a few eras**. Example: as of now Axemen obsolete at Civil Service can still be useful through Medieval, but can be scrapped from Renaissance; Knights obsolete in Renaissance can remain useful through Renaissance, but can be scrapped from Industrial. **Cargo-capable units are still kept**. The rationale is that only very outdated units are no longer useful enough to justify their clutter or upkeep; until then, keeping units is usually better than short-term financial relief from scrapping, because they can defend cities, deter attacks, pressure rivals, or be spent in war. War can also reduce excess units naturally, and successful captures can increase unit support, economy, and long-term growth more than deleting troops would. So this strict-but-not-absolute scrapping gate is believed to be stronger for AI (at least in theory; in autoplay it does not seem weaker at a glance and based on the now enhanced BBAI logging we added as well).
 
