ttleHistory.py), [CvEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/CvEventManager.py), [BugEventManager.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/BugEventManager.py), [CvUnit.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvUnit.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.cpp), [CvDllPythonEvents.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvDllPythonEvents.h), [CvEventReporter.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.cpp), [CvEventReporter.h](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvEventReporter.h).
 - Added a new **Summary tab** in the Military Advisor, showing a **synthetic view** of our Military: **Support** (detailed Cost and Supply, and Unit Cap numerical breakdown (e.g., `P x R x M    (1 x 100 x 82) / 10000 = 0 gold icon char`), Military Buildings, Military Production (some not shown for concision as panel is mostly full) and XP information, and Allied Hammers for total hammer value of allies' (e.g., vassals, same team) army); **Army** (detailed numerical overview for military/civilian units, Domain repartition (Land/Sea/Air), Strongest, Costliest, Total/Avg Hammers as a power estimation of units, Power Rank (Known) (e.g., `9/11` (in fact `44/48` if debug mode is enabled for spoilers)), Top promotions, Covert Units (Invisible, Spies, Hidden Nationality), And upgradeable units costs (Min/Avg/Max/Total)); **Deployment** (Allied/Neutral/Enemy Cities/Territory/Roaming information with Avg Defense and Best defense of our cities, defensive buildings (as of now Walls and Castles (e.g., `1 / 2`)), Wounded information (Max/Avg/Min and Full/High/Medium/Low Health (e.g, `15 (100%)`)), and Battles reusing the [SASBattleHistory.py](/Assets/Python/SASBattleHistory.py) added with the new Battles Tab (Won/Retreated/Lost (e.g., `35 (33%)`)), Good-Luck Wins and Bad-Luck Losses counts (`e.g., 11 (31%)`), Best/Worst (e.g., `6.3 vs 10.0 1300 AD (39%)`)). Also added a **legend link**.
 - Added a new **Composition Tab**, as a set of **sortable tables** for **Current** (unlike saved data in the Statistics Tab in the Info Screen) **Units** (non-civilian, including Animal (including Barbarian in debug mode)), **Promotions**, and **Unit Combats** **counts**, default-**sorted from most to least** for no tedium (as done in the Statistics Tab). See also [KI#129](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#129---fixed-military-advisor-map-tab-minimap-disappeared-after-switching-tabs).

